(
    // Cromatolis-only wildlife-density multiplier (see
    // `world/src/layer/wildlife.rs`'s `cromatolis_wildlife_boost`), applied
    // on top of every manifest entry's own density formula, but only for
    // chunks inside the authored Cromatolis region -- every other world
    // using this engine is completely unaffected by this file.
    //
    // Calibrated against a real `World::generate_chunk`-instrumented audit
    // (the full roll+gradient+footprint-clearance entity-placement
    // pipeline, not just the density formula): land was measured at 1.26%
    // of real chunks producing any wildlife entity, open ocean at 6.39% --
    // both read as far too sparse during normal exploration. These two
    // values were tuned (one round of measure-and-adjust) to bring both to
    // a real chunk-hit-rate of roughly 20%, landing at 18.37% (land) and
    // 18.63% (ocean) on the final audit run. Lake was already measured at
    // 43.88% and is intentionally left unboosted (`world/src/layer/
    // wildlife.rs` never reads an `ocean`-style field for it) -- see the
    // commit that introduced this file for the exact numbers.
    land: 24.0,
    ocean: 3.2,
)
